{
  "id": "T-7",
  "question": "Does a hit on a weak point that breaks shields let all of the rest through to health?",
  "bible": "§10",
  "gameVersion": "44.1.4.1",
  "reports": [
    {
      "on": "2026-11-27",
      "words": "| Level | Colour | On the shield | On health | Did it die? |\n| 100 | white | 8007 | 27958 | no (~5% health left) |\n| 100 | yellow | 8007 | 72052 | yes |\n| 150 | white | 10881 | 22210 | no (~40% health left) |\n| 150 | yellow | 10881 | 66304 | yes |"
    },
    {
      "on": "2026-11-27",
      "words": "The Crewman has a helmet that breaks off visually, I think that might be the 100 health entity we see. It only breaks once shields are broken."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Asked for in the Simulacrum with AI paused, Steel Path off, a fresh plain Crewman for every shot, the T-46 Lanka build (Serration, Radiated Reload, Primed Bane of Corpus, Stormbringer, Hellfire, Critical Delay, all at max), charged and unscoped at the head from about 10 m, with no aura, arcanes, companion, abilities or shards, and no numbers were predicted to Pavel. The shield shows what it had left, 8,007 and 10,881 (whole shields, T-46), so the head lets all of the rest through: under the 5% gate the level 100 white would show about 21,300 on it. Health loses all of the rest too: 14,029 of 15,207.5 leaves 7.7% at level 100, and 11,155 of 19,019.3 leaves 41% at 150, which Pavel put at about 5% and 40%; the yellows kill. The yellows show no headcrit on a Crewman's head, as the library has it: with one, the level 100 yellow would show about 160,000. The numbers on health have no case: each is twice what health took less 100 (27,958 = 2 × 14,029.1 − 100, and so are the other three, to the digit), which is T-43's number for a hit that breaks a part: the Crewman's helmet, which Pavel sees break off, and only once the shields are gone. It has 100 at levels 100 and 150 alike. That needs parts with health of their own (ABA-59). Lanka's charged shot is in the fixture, with Radiated Reload, for the reason in T-38.",
